# Copy this file to `.env.llm` and fill in real values:
#
#   cp .env.llm.example .env.llm
#
# `.env.llm` is gitignored (this template is not) and is picked up
# automatically by `capmap agent` -- it walks up from the instance directory
# to find the closest `.env.llm`, so one shared file at the repo root or a
# per-instance override both work. A real shell `export` always takes
# priority over anything in the file.
#
# capmap agent talks to any endpoint that speaks the OpenAI /chat/completions
# wire format -- see README.md's "对话式操作：capmap agent" section for the full picture.

# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# OPENAI_API_KEY=<your-api-key>
# OPENAI_MODEL=<model-id-exactly-as-your-endpoint-expects-it>   # no default -- deployment-specific

# --- optional: only if your gateway wants the key on a non-standard header
# --- too (Portkey does -- set it to x-portkey-api-key). Most OpenAI-compatible
# --- endpoints authenticate fine with the standard Bearer header alone.
# OPENAI_EXTRA_HEADER=x-portkey-api-key

# --- to reach Claude instead, point at Anthropic's own beta OpenAI-compatible
# --- endpoint (a migration-oriented subset of its native API -- no extended
# --- thinking, some params silently dropped):
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com/v1
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# OPENAI_MODEL=claude-opus-5
